    "note": "Byte for byte the good SN2 with a spectator counterion, except that both justification strings are empty. The chemistry is correct and every other check stays green: mass, charge, and valence electrons all balance, the two arrows account for every structural change, no hydrogen moves, and sodium really is identical on both sides. Only the record keeping is broken. fixture-schema.ts documents that the parser reads justification with asString rather than asNonEmptyString for exactly this fixture, because a parser that rejected an empty justification would make this negative control unwritable and conservation-spectator-declaration could never be shown to fire on its hygiene arm. Two violations, one per state. declaredBy is left populated so the failing line is unambiguously about the missing justification and not about ownership."
  },
